{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS reduces publishing time for Carbon Footprint Data to 21 days or Less - AWS","context":"AWS has significantly reduced the publishing time for carbon footprint data from up to three months to 21 days or less. This improvement provides users with more timely insights into their carbon emissions and resource usage. The Carbon Footprint Tool (CCFT) dashboard now offers carbon footprint data with estimates published between the 15th and 21st of the month following usage. Additionally, the CCFT dashboard maintains 38 months of data, enabling users to view their carbon usage trends over an extended period. To access the carbon footprint data, users can navigate to their carbon emissions data through the AWS Billing and Cost Management console. For further information about CCFT, users can visit the CCFT capabilities and features page, review the user guides, and explore the CCFT webpage","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/12/aws-reduces-publishing-time-carbon-footprint-data/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS launches Sustainability console for carbon emissions tracking - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced the AWS Sustainability console, a new, standalone service that enables sustainability professionals to access carbon emissions data from their AWS usage without requiring billing permissions. This service builds upon the features of the Customer Carbon Footprint Tool (CCFT) in the AWS Billing console. The console provides customers with their estimated carbon emissions from using AWS, calculated using market-based and location-based methods, and available by AWS Region, service, and emissions scope (1, 2, 3). Additional capabilities include customizable visualizations, the ability to set the fiscal year start month, customizable CSV reports, and API/SDK access for seamless integration of emissions data into existing reporting workflows. The AWS Sustainability console is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia) region and provides carbon emissions data for all AWS commercial regions","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/03/aws-launches-sustainability-console/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS’ Customer Carbon Footprint Tool now includes Scope 3 emissions data - AWS","context":"AWS has updated its Customer Carbon Footprint Tool (CCFT) to include Scope 3 emissions data and Scope 1 natural gas and refrigerants. This expansion allows AWS customers to have a more comprehensive view of their cloud carbon footprint, covering all three industry-standard emission scopes as defined by the Greenhouse Gas Protocol. The update provides visibility into the lifecycle carbon impact of AWS usage, including emissions from manufacturing servers, powering AWS facilities, and transporting equipment to data centers. Historical data is available from January 2022, enabling organizations to track their progress and make informed decisions about their cloud strategy to meet sustainability goals. The updated CCFT data is accessible through the dashboard and AWS Billing and Cost Management Data Exports, allowing for easy integration into operational workflows, sustainability planning, and reporting processes. For more information, visit the AWS Billing and Cost Management console or read the updated methodology documentation and release notes","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/aws-customer-carbon-footprint-tool-scope-3-emissions-data/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-marketplace-metering","skill_description":"Deploys, queries, and debugs AWS Marketplace usage-based (PAYG) metering — the pipeline (ResolveCustomer, BatchMeterUsage, EventBridge via SAM) and querying/debugging metering records, statuses, failures, discrepancies. Covers Concurrent Agreements (CustomerAWSAccountId + LicenseArn), multi-product, CloudTrail Event History (90 days; never CloudTrail Lake), Seller Reports (Billed Revenue/Usage columns + CSV/SDDS parsing), existing-stack detection, metering region for BatchMeterUsage/MeterUsage (DisabledApiException), metered AMI/Container + IAM roles, where registration data lives (customer-profile table), legacy ProductCode + CustomerIdentifier, DuplicateRecord/CustomerNotSubscribed, bad LicenseArn. Also SCOPES adjacent asks — flat-rate/SaaS-Subscription \"do I still meter\", CCP included-units + overage, contract term/annual renewal, forecasting future bills/usage — with the right answer or a one-line redirect. Use for any BatchMeterUsage/ResolveCustomer or SaaS usage-billing question.\n\nServices: aws-marketplace, marketplace-metering\nTasks: deploy, integrate, query, debug, troubleshoot, analyze\nPersona: developer\nWorkload: saas\n*","skill_name":"aws-marketplace-metering"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"timestream-influxdb","skill_description":"Retrieves authoritative guidance on Amazon Timestream for InfluxDB across its supported engine variants. Applicable to any InfluxDB-on-AWS request including engine variant and licensing selection, provisioning and IAM, encryption at rest (AWS-owned and customer-managed KMS keys, key policies, and key lifecycle), schema design (tags vs fields, cardinality, HTTP/sensor/metric data modeling), migration from LiveAnalytics, Processing Engine plugins, connectivity (database endpoints and private or public access), and write/query errors.\n\nServices: timestream, timestream-influxdb, influxdb\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, migrate, monitor, model\nPersona: developer, devops, operator, architect, data-engineer\nWorkload: time-series, iot, observability, metrics, sensor-data\n*","skill_name":"timestream-influxdb"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS Carbon Footprint Tool API documentation for GetCarbonFootprintSummary details."}
